},
["03:42"]={
{"The phone rang at \0033:42 a.m.\004 Who could be calling this late? Or rather, “this early?” They’d only been asleep for a few hours. Easter Vigil had ended around 11 p.m. and she had then gotten everything ready for the Easter Sunrise Service, which would begin around 6 a.m.","Blood Stained","Gayl Siegel",true},
{"Let’s see what those search warrants yield. So far Pelley has admitted he was at the bonfire. The lab says his boot imprints are a match to the marks on Leena’s body. Pelley cannot account for the time between when he was last seen leaving the bonfire with his arm around Leena and when he arrived home at \0033:42 a.m.\004 in a severely inebriated state, according to his wife, Lacey.","Beneath Devil’s Bridge","Loreth Anne White",true},
{"We are due in Yellow Sky at \0033:42\004, he said, looking tenderly into her eyes.\n“Oh, are we?” she said, as if she had not been aware of it. To evince surprise at her husband’s statement was part of her wifely amiability.","Bride Comes to Yellow Sky","Stephen Crane",true},
},
["03:43"]={
{"The clock says \0033:43 am\004. The thermometer says it’s a chilly fourteen degrees Fahrenheit. The weatherman says the cold spell will last until Thursday, so bundle up and bundle up some more. There are icicles barring the window of the bat cave.","Ghostwritten","David Mitchell",true},
},
["03:44"]={
{"When I opened my eyes, an oyster-colored dawn was peeping in at the windows. The hands of my brass alarm clock stood at \0033:44\004.","The Sweetness at the Bottom of the Pie","Alan Bradley",true},
{"It was dark. After she had switched the light on and been to the toilet, she checked her watch: \0033:44 a.m.\004 She undressed, put the cat out the door and returned to the twin bed.","Liver: Leberknödel","Will Self",true},
},
["03:45"]={
{"He touched the face of his watch to check the time: \00303:45\004. The code that would open the outer door and allow him to descend to the safety of his other world.","Over My Dead Body","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"Abra did not quiet. The crying was monotonous, maddening, terrifying. When they arrived at Bridgton Hospital, it was \003quarter of four\004, and Abra was still at full volume. Rides in the Acura were usually better than a sleeping pill, but not this morning.","Doctor Sleep","Stephen King",true},
{"LORD CAVERSHAM: Well, sir! what are you doing here? Wasting your life as usual! You should be in bed, sir. You keep too late hours! I heard of you the other night at Lady Rufford’s dancing till four o’clock in the morning!\nLORD GORING: Only a \003quarter to four\004, father.","An Ideal Husband","Oscar Wilde",true},
},
["03:46"]={
